config: Honkai: Star Rail gets the GPU identity of Genshin Impact and Zenless Zone Zero

DXMT has a built-in setting for GenshinImpact.exe, YuanShen.exe and ZenlessZoneZero.exe that
reports the GPU as an AMD Radeon Pro 5300M (vendor 1002, device 7340), the graphics of an Intel
MacBook Pro. StarRail.exe was not in the list, so the game was told "Apple M5" with vendor and
device id 0 (its Player.log: "Renderer: Apple M5 (ID=0x0)" and a vendor name that is not text).

The game's engine got past creating its Direct3D device with that, so this is not known to be
why it failed to start; it removes a difference from the two games that do. See Wine runtime
patch 0057 for what the game needs to start at all.

diff --git a/src/util/config/config.cpp b/src/util/config/config.cpp
--- a/src/util/config/config.cpp
+++ b/src/util/config/config.cpp
@@ -41,7 +41,9 @@
 
 
   const static ProfileList g_profiles = {{
-    { R"(\\(GenshinImpact|YuanShen|ZenlessZoneZero)\.exe$)", {{
+    /* FineWine: Honkai: Star Rail gets the identity its two sister games get. Without it the
+     * game is told "Apple M5" with vendor and device id 0. */
+    { R"(\\(GenshinImpact|YuanShen|ZenlessZoneZero|StarRail)\.exe$)", {{
       { "dxgi.customDeviceDesc",   "AMD Radeon Pro 5300M" },
       { "dxgi.customVendorId",     "1002" },
       { "dxgi.customDeviceId",     "7340" },
